  "finish": {
    "summary": "Five drawers in one base isn't possible here. One base can hold at most one drawer. The build is now a single north-half hex base with one drawer in it, and the checks pass with no collisions.",
    "requirements": [
      {
        "requirement": "A single hex base, nothing else beside or on top",
        "status": "met",
        "evidence": "Only piece:0,0,0;half-n plus the drawer inside it. I swapped the full base for a half because a full base can't take drawers."
      },
      {
        "requirement": "Five drawers in the base",
        "status": "unmet",
        "evidence": "Drawers only fit on the cut face of a half base, and the configurator offered just one place for one (slot s, in every style I tried). A full base and a quarter base offered none. After adding drawer:0#0,0#cut, no more places were offered. So 1 of 5."
      }
    ]
